id: pm-csv-qebc
title: Failed atomic create compensation erases orphan reconciliation markers
description: "Greptile's exact-head review of PR 73 found that compensateCreate removed csv-tx and csv-txrow ownership markers before attempting pm close. If close then failed, the item remained open but could no longer be located by transaction id. Close first, preserve markers on any failed close, clean markers only after confirmed terminal state, and make the public atomic contract disclose best-effort compensation and reconciliation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: atomic,compensation,reconciliation,review
created_at: "2026-08-20T20:05:53.614Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T20:12:59.876Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T20:08:47.032Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T20:08:47.032Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 75
acceptance_criteria: "A red regression proves failed close preserves both transaction markers; Compensation closes before removing markers; No nonzero close receipt, including exit 4, is treated as proof of closure; A marker-cleanup failure is logged and leaves a closed marked item discoverable; Public README, option type, example, and flag describe best-effort compensation, intentionally non-reverted pre-existing updates, and inspect-and-reconcile guidance; npm run release:check passes exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and every repository-owned quality gate; strict workspace health reports the separately tracked published pm-github manifest blocker"
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: critical
repro_steps: "Create a transaction-marked item, force pm close to fail, call compensateCreate, then inspect the still-open item tags."
resolution: "Close an open item before removing csv-tx ownership markers; return with markers intact on close failure, and report marker cleanup failure after a successful or already-terminal close. Align README and extension metadata with best-effort compensation and explicit reconciliation."
expected_result: A failed close leaves the open item transaction-marked and discoverable; successful or already-closed compensation removes the markers; public docs require reconciliation.
actual_result: "The implementation now closes first, preserves both markers on failed close, logs failed marker cleanup while leaving a closed marked item discoverable, and removes all atomic all-or-nothing promises from public contracts."
affected_version: 2026.8.16
fixed_version: unreleased
component: atomic-import
regression: true
